29806:
Disproportionation needs the central atom to both oxidise and reduce itself
Chlorine oxidation states here run +1 and +3 and +5 up to +7 in \text{ClO}_4^{-}
At +7 chlorine cannot oxidise further, so \text{ClO}_4^{-} cannot disproportionate → (B)

