29812:
Dissolution gives 3 \text{Zr}^{4+} and 4 \text{PO}_4^{3-} per formula unit
With solubility s, K_{sp} = (3s)^{3} (4s)^{4} = 27 \times 256 s^{7} = 6912 s^{7}
Hence s = (\frac{K_{sp}}{6912})^{1/7} → (A)

29818:
\text{CrO}_2\text{Cl}_2 in \text{CS}_2 followed by hydrolysis is the Etard oxidation of toluene to benzaldehyde \text{PhCHO}
\text{NaHSO}_3 adds to the aldehyde giving residue (A) = \text{PhCH(OH)SO}_3\text{Na}
Dilute HCl regenerates the aldehyde, so compound (B) = \text{PhCHO}
Row showing adduct (A) with aldehyde (B) is labelled (4) → (D)

